This is happening because of a classic React "stale state" race condition in your frontend code.
When your page loads, both of your useEffect hooks fire immediately. The first one extracts the auth data and calls setCurrentRoleId(). However, React state updates are asynchronous. By the time your second useEffect calls fetchInitialData(), the currentRoleId variable is still null.
Because it passes roleId=null to your backend, your backend is likely ignoring the WHERE clause and returning *all* VIDs instead of restricting them to the specific role.
To fix this, we need to extract the roleId synchronously straight from local storage right before making the API call, completely bypassing the React state race condition.
### The Fix (VoucherPosting.js)
Find your second useEffect block (around line 185) and replace the **entire fetchInitialData function** with this highly secure version:
```javascript
  useEffect(() => {
    const fetchInitialData = async () => {
      try {
        setIsPageLoading(true);

        // CRITICAL FIX: Synchronously extract the role directly from storage. 
        // Do not rely on 'currentRoleId' state here, as it will be 'null' on the first render.
        let actualRoleId = null;
        const auth = sessionStorage.getItem("persist:auth") || localStorage.getItem("persist:auth");
        if (auth) {
          const user = JSON.parse(JSON.parse(auth).user);
          // Checks multiple common property names just to be safe
          actualRoleId = user?.roleId || user?.role || user?.ROLE_ID; 
        }

        if (!actualRoleId) {
          showSnackBar("Security Error: User Role ID not found. Cannot fetch VIDs.", "error");
          setIsPageLoading(false);
          return; // Aborts the call if no role is found
        }

        // Passes the guaranteed correct role ID to the backend
        const vouchersResponse = await callApi(`/JS/voucher/active?roleId=${actualRoleId}`, null, "GET");

         // Defensively extract the array whether your callApi unwraps the { data: [...] } or not
        if (vouchersResponse && Array.isArray(vouchersResponse.data)) {
          setVoucherList(vouchersResponse.data);
        } else if (Array.isArray(vouchersResponse)) {
          setVoucherList(vouchersResponse);
        } else {
          setVoucherList([]); // Safe fallback
        }

        // 1. FIRST: Check the EOD Status from your new API
        const eodResponse = await callApi("/JS/voucher/eod_status", null, "GET");

        // The API returns an array: [{ "eodStatus": 0 }]
        if (eodResponse && Array.isArray(eodResponse) && eodResponse.length > 0) {
          if (eodResponse[0].eodStatus === 1) {
            setIsEodRunning(true);
            setIsPageLoading(false);
            return; // STOP loading everything else, block the screen
          }
        }

        // 2. IF EOD IS NOT RUNNING: Continue loading the normal page data
        const dateResponse = await callApi("/JS/voucher/current-posting-date", null, "GET");

        if (dateResponse) {
          try {
            const [year, month, day] = dateResponse.split("-");
            const formattedDate = `${day}-${month}-${year}`;
            setPostingDate(formattedDate);
          } catch (e) {
            console.error("Could not parse date:", dateResponse, e);
            setPostingDate(dateResponse);
          }
        } else {
          showSnackBar("Failed to load official posting date.", "error");
          setPostingDate("Error");
        }

        const currencyResponse = await callApi("/CM/common-master/currency", null, "GET");
        if (currencyResponse?.success && Array.isArray(currencyResponse.data)) {
          let uniqueCurrencies = [...new Set(currencyResponse.data)];
          
          // Sort the array so "INR" is always at index 0, and the rest are alphabetical
          uniqueCurrencies.sort((a, b) => {
            if (a === "INR") return -1;
            if (b === "INR") return 1;
            return a.localeCompare(b);
          });
          
          setCurrencyOptions(uniqueCurrencies);
        } else {
          showSnackBar("Failed to load currencies.", "error");
        }

      } catch (error) {
        console.error("Error fetching initial data:", error);
        showSnackBar("An error occurred while loading page data.", "error");
      } finally {
        setIsPageLoading(false);
      }
    };

    fetchInitialData();
  }, [callApi, showSnackBar]);

```
### A Quick Backend Security Note
While fixing the frontend solves the immediate UI bug, your backend API (/JS/voucher/active) should theoretically extract the role ID securely from the JWT token (using jwtUtil.getUserRoleFromToken(token)) rather than trusting a URL parameter (?roleId=X). Relying strictly on the JWT token prevents malicious users from manually altering the URL to view unauthorized VIDs.
